PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F139A1768696898
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G1/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe junction where the CBBC
OL,4,Cpresenter was the BBC One announcer
OL,5,
OL,6,FARCHIVE: YouTube: Doubledeckers
OL,7,
OL,8,FEvery so often the past throws up
OL,9,Flittle mysteries.  Sometimes they are
OL,10,Fvery trivial in themselves but can
OL,11,Fstill be a fascinating insight into a
OL,12,Fbygone era.
OL,13,
OL,14,FOne of these mysteries concerns the
OL,15,F5.35pm junction on BBC One on a handful
OL,16,Fof occasions between 1985 and 1988.
OL,17,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBRewindCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,200,120,120,200,0,100
PN,13902
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F139A1768696898
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G2/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe junction where the CBBC
OL,4,Cpresenter was the BBC One announcer
OL,5,
OL,6,FAs all Pres fans of a certain age will
OL,7,Fremember, this junction was not voiced
OL,8,Fby the regular announcer.  Instead
OL,9,FPhillip Schofield, Andy Crane and the
OL,10,Fother CBBC presenters would do the
OL,11,Flink.
OL,12,
OL,13,FClearly this was an editorial decision
OL,14,F` not just an operational necessity
OL,15,Fbecause they were in the broom
OL,16,Fcupboard.
OL,17,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBRewindCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,200,120,120,200,0,100
PN,13903
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F139A1768696898
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G3/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe junction where the CBBC
OL,4,Cpresenter was the BBC One announcer
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt would have been easy enough for the
OL,7,Fregular announcer to record a link or
OL,8,Fuse the lip mic which was apparently
OL,9,Flocated in the main NC1 control room
OL,10,Ffor emergencies. (This happened
OL,11,Fregularly during the link before CBBC
OL,12,Fat 3.50pm after the start of the new
OL,13,Fdaytime schedule in 1986 when the
OL,14,Fregional news stopped providing a
OL,15,Fbuffer.)
OL,16,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBRewindCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,200,120,120,200,0,100
PN,13904
SC,0004
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F139A1768696898
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G4/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe junction where the CBBC
OL,4,Cpresenter was the BBC One announcer
OL,5,
OL,6,FCreatively, it was always a little
OL,7,Fawkward having the CBBC presenter link
OL,8,Finto the 5.35pm programme. In those
OL,9,Fdays, the voice behind the globe really
OL,10,Fdid help to establish the authority of
OL,11,Fthe BBC.
OL,12,
OL,13,FBut when the link was simply into The
OL,14,FFlintstones, Cartoon Time or the
OL,15,Fschools quiz First Class it hardly
OL,16,Fmattered in practice.
OL,17,
OL,18,FIt was maybe more of an issue when the
OL,19,F5.35pm programme was not particularly
OL,20,Fchild friendly ` say Masterteam.
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBRewindCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,200,120,120,200,0,100
PN,13905
SC,0005
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F139A1768696898
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G5/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe junction where the CBBC
OL,4,Cpresenter was the BBC One announcer
OL,5,
OL,6,FBut what about the occasions when a
OL,7,Fsignificant or important programme was
OL,8,Fbeing shown at 5.35pm?
OL,9,
OL,10,FDuring the 1986 Mexico World Cup,
OL,11,FPhillip was allowed to link into the
OL,12,Fregular highlights programme shown
OL,13,Fbetween CBBC and the Six o'Clock News.
OL,14,
OL,15,FOuch.
OL,16,
OL,17,FYou can begin to see why some in
OL,18,FPresentation were apparently less than
OL,19,Fkeen on having someone who wasn't an
OL,20,Fannouncer in the continuity suite.
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBRewindCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,200,120,120,200,0,100
PN,13906
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F139A1768696898
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G6/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe junction where the CBBC
OL,4,Cpresenter was the BBC One announcer
OL,5,
OL,6,FBut here's an even bigger question.
OL,7,
OL,8,FThere were a few occasions between 1985
OL,9,Fand 1987 when the regional news moved
OL,10,Fto 5.35pm to accommodate extended
OL,11,Feditions of the Six o'Clock News or
OL,12,Fother special output.
OL,13,
OL,14,FOutside London and the South East, of
OL,15,Fcourse, there would have been a
OL,16,Fstandard opt-out link.
OL,17,
OL,18,FBut what was happening in NC1 Con?
OL,19,FWere Phillip and Andy really linking
OL,20,Finto London Plus?
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBRewindCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,200,120,120,200,0,100
PN,13907
SC,0007
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F139A1768696898
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G7/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe junction where the CBBC
OL,4,Cpresenter was the BBC One announcer
OL,5,
OL,6,FYou can begin to see why this could
OL,7,Fhave been an issue.
OL,8,
OL,9,FAn announcement before the news by
OL,10,Fsomeone who didn't represent the
OL,11,Fauthority of the BBC, a real handbrake
OL,12,Fturn from the fun in the broom
OL,13,Fcupboard, a voice quite unlike that of
OL,14,Fthe announcers of the time.
OL,15,
OL,16,FSo does anyone know what happened?
OL,17,
OL,18,FA very trivial mystery from a long time
OL,19,Fago needs resolved.
OL,20,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBRewindCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,200,120,120,200,0,100@
